293	  <p class="lead">Hooke's law on strain plus a dashpot along the spring — equal and opposite on the two ends</p>
294	  <div class="content">
295	    <div class="two">
296	      <div style="flex:none;width:500px">
297	        <p class="sub-h">Unit direction and strain</p>
298	        <div class="eq sm">\[\mathbf d=\frac{\mathbf x_j-\mathbf x_i}{\lVert\mathbf x_j-\mathbf x_i\rVert},\qquad \varepsilon=\frac{\lVert\mathbf x_j-\mathbf x_i\rVert}{L_0}-1\]</div>
299	        <p class="sub-h">Spring + axial dashpot</p>
300	        <div class="eqbox"><div class="eq sm">\[\mathbf F_{ij}=k\,\varepsilon\,\mathbf d+c\,\big[(\mathbf v_j-\mathbf v_i)\cdot\mathbf d\big]\,\mathbf d\]</div></div>
301	        <div class="eq sm">\[\mathbf f_i\mathrel{+}=\mathbf F_{ij},\qquad \mathbf f_j\mathrel{-}=\mathbf F_{ij}\]</div>
302	        <p class="def">\(k\) multiplies a <i>strain</i>, so it acts like \(E\cdot A\), not N/m. Dashpot \(c=100\).</p>
303	      </div>
