856	<section class="slide" data-title="Summary">
857	  <p class="lead">A rope twin is springs + one velocity-level contact law, run 667 times per frame</p>
858	  <div class="content">
859	    <ul class="lec">
860	      <li><b>Simulation model</b> : log-stiffness springs with axial dashpots, exponential drag, symplectic Euler at 50 µs
861	        <ul><li>\(\Delta t\) is set by the stiffest, shortest spring — 1.7× below the limit</li></ul></li>
862	      <li><b>Boundary condition</b> : PhysTwin welds the hand with springs; real2sim-eval uses a moving mesh with friction
863	        <ul><li>only the second can slip, drop, and be a fair test of a grasp</li></ul></li>
864	      <li><b>Contact model</b> : \(\mathbf v_n'=-e\mathbf v_n,\ \mathbf v_t'=a\mathbf v_t\) for ground, self and mesh
865	        <ul><li>Coulomb friction as a velocity scale factor, plus position projection</li></ul></li>
866	      <li><b>Cost</b> : on a GPU, launches and refits dominate — not arithmetic, not the broad phase</li>
867	      <li><b>Consequence</b> : <span class="red">contact turns float round-off into mm-scale divergence</span> — budget for it in RL and system ID</li>
868	    </ul>
